  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0051","idiomatic","After the Kaiyao era, a Guizhou intra-circuit frontier commissioner was appointed, commanding fourteen prefectures—Gui, Wu, He, Lian, Liu, Fu, Zhao, Meng, Yan, Huanrong, Gu, Sitang, and Gong—from his seat at Guizhou.","After the Kaiyao era, a Guizhou intra-circuit frontier commissioner was appointed, commanding fourteen prefectures—Gui, Wu, He, Lian, Liu, Fu, Zhao, Meng, Yan, Huan, Rong, Gu, Sitang, and Gong—from his seat at Guizhou.","Chinese 領…十四州 enumerates fourteen prefectures; with 環融 kept as one name the list has only thirteen. Splitting 環融 into 環 and 融 yields fourteen single-name prefectures matching the stated total; English Huanrong must become Huan, Rong.","high","applied"],
    ["s0051","literal","After Kaiyao, a Guizhou intra-circuit frontier commissioner was established, holding Gui, Wu, He, Lian, Liu, Fu, Zhao, Meng, Yan, Huanrong, Gu, Sitang, and Gong prefectures—fourteen in all—with seat at Guizhou.","After Kaiyao, a Guizhou intra-circuit frontier commissioner was established, holding Gui, Wu, He, Lian, Liu, Fu, Zhao, Meng, Yan, Huan, Rong, Gu, Sitang, and Gong prefectures—fourteen in all—with seat at Guizhou.","Same unit: 十四州 requires fourteen names; 環融 is two prefectures (環、融) omitted as a separator in the Chinese list. Literal Huanrong is the fused error; Huan, Rong restores the count and naming.","high","applied"]
  ],
